00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:52.265
or four years ago, I'm not sure,

00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:55.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
but what is it about
you do you think

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:58.604
that lets you be brave in
these very strange times?

00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:01.541
Because I think the reason
you've made a mark suddenly

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:03.276 align:start size:88% position:13%
is people are like,
"Oh, that girl is saying

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:06.546
what she thinks, and so many
people are afraid to do it",

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.881
some guy wrote a
book about that.

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:10.516
- (chuckles) He did, he did,

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:11.984
and we're actually
reading that book

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my community right now.
- Very, very serious.

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:17.123
- But I think what,
what for me is...

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:19.892 align:start position:0%
I mean, frankly what is lacking
among so many of the people

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.093
that we see out protesting

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:23.195 align:start size:88% position:13%
that all want these
safe spaces is I've had

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:25.264
to overcome a lot of
challenges in my life

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:28.568
from my family to different
bullies I've met in my life

00:09:28.568 --> 00:09:31.771 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think that when you
overcome challenges like that,

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.606
it sets you up to take on things

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:36.809
that are much more important.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:39.378 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I think that I've developed
the resiliency from having,

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.213
to overcome things
throughout my life,

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.316 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I don't mind
standing up on a stage

00:09:43.316 --> 00:09:44.850
and saying, "This
is what I think,

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.786
this is why I walked away
from the Democratic Party,

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:48.020
and some people
are gonna like it

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.221
and some people are
going to hate it,

00:09:49.221 --> 00:09:50.690
and that's just the way it is",

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also think that
there's something to being

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.961
in this every day, isn't there?

00:09:54.961 --> 00:09:57.663
Is that when you have
the hate come at you,

00:09:57.663 --> 00:10:00.199
it's a pattern and you can see
that no matter what you say,

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:01.400
no matter what you do,

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.536 align:start size:84% position:16%
the hate comes in
exactly the same way,

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:05.071
is incredibly predictable.

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:06.572
And so after a while you start

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:09.108
to realize it has nothing
to do with you at all.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:11.043
It has to do with them
and where they're at

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.545
and the goals that they have

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:15.047
and trying to achieve those
goals by any means necessary.

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:16.682
So I can't take it personally,

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:18.117
it's not about me,
it's about them.

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.819
- Yeah, it's funny I had a tweet

00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:21.020
that was catching fire today

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:24.223 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I had a very,
very minor typo in it

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:27.727 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I had like hundreds
of these trolls,

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.829 align:start size:84% position:16%
did you have a stroke,
are you retarded,

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:31.230 align:start size:84% position:16%
like stuff that's
much worse than that

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.200
and it's like, I don't
really care about that,

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.735
but it's like, wait a minute,

00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:38.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought you guys were
the tolerant, good people,

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:41.941
but maybe not as
tolerant and good

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:44.510
as you say you are
something like that.

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:48.781
Where do you sense
your community going,

00:10:48.781 --> 00:10:51.951
what's the goal and how do you
stay out of the echo chamber?

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:53.219 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, one of the
things that I'm trying

00:10:53.219 --> 00:10:55.154
to figure out with
my own community is

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:57.657
that people are paying a
couple of bucks to get in,

00:10:57.657 --> 00:10:59.492
so you're self-selecting a
certain amount of people,

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:00.826
and I know for people like us,

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:02.895
we don't want it to be
just like minded people

00:11:02.895 --> 00:11:04.897
and I love seeing people
interact with each other

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:06.132
and agree to disagree,

00:11:06.132 --> 00:11:08.634 align:start size:84% position:16%
but how do you
guard against that?

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:13.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I really wanna have more
constructive discussion

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:14.840 align:start size:88% position:13%
and constructive
debate in my community.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.208
One of the things
that I found is

00:11:16.208 --> 00:11:18.644
that it is incredibly
hard to get people

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:20.279
who are not Trump supporters

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:22.314
or people on the right
to join the community.

00:11:22.314 --> 00:11:24.216
We do have lefties in
there and I'm grateful

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:25.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they're in there
and I'm grateful

00:11:25.751 --> 00:11:28.054
for their contribution, but I
really wanna see more of them.

00:11:28.054 --> 00:11:29.522
So one of the things I wanna do

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:30.890
when I have a little downtime

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.426
after the election is
I wanna start doing

00:11:33.426 --> 00:11:35.094
more constructive discussions,

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:36.595
I wanna start a debate club.

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:37.997
I actually wanna
have a debate club

00:11:37.997 --> 00:11:39.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people get assigned
to their position

00:11:39.432 --> 00:11:40.833
so they don't get
to choose them,

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:42.068
so sometimes they might have

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:43.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
to argue positions
they don't agree with,

00:11:43.969 --> 00:11:45.905 align:start size:81% position:19%
just to understand
the other side.

00:11:45.905 --> 00:11:48.674 align:start position:0%
And I think it's very important
for people to demonstrate

00:11:48.674 --> 00:11:51.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're capable of
having adult conversations

00:11:51.143 --> 00:11:53.612
and walking away and being
like it's okay to disagree,

00:11:53.612 --> 00:11:55.181
it's okay, we're
all gonna survive

00:11:55.181 --> 00:11:57.349
- It's weird to be one
of the adults in the room

00:11:57.349 --> 00:12:00.086 align:start size:97% position:3%
when there aren't as many
adults in the room, isn't it?

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:03.022
- Well, I'll tell you, if
you looked at my Twitter,

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:04.490
you would not think I was one
of the adults in the room,

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.792
but I do really try to
be in real life. (laughs)

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:10.629
- Well, I don't know what says
about the state of adulthood

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:13.966 align:start size:97% position:3%
like I'm making as many Star
Wars in GI Joe references

00:12:13.966 --> 00:12:16.168
and yet somehow I'm
an adult in the room,

00:12:16.168 --> 00:12:17.369
that's not 'cause of me,

00:12:17.369 --> 00:12:18.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's mostly 'cause
of these people.

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.741 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I mean,
that's a reflection

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:23.609 align:start size:97% position:3%
of where the people we're
fighting at are, aren't they?

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:25.077
Because if were the
adults in the room,

00:12:25.077 --> 00:12:27.513 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, they're
the kindergarteners

00:12:27.513 --> 00:12:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the room, aren't they?
- Yeah.

00:12:28.748 --> 00:12:29.982
- All right, so one
more question for you

00:12:29.982 --> 00:12:31.484
and then I want you to
pimp out your community

00:12:31.484 --> 00:12:33.219
as hardcore as you can.

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:38.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
What do you see as the
path to getting out

00:12:38.224 --> 00:12:40.893 align:start size:88% position:13%
of the mess that we
all feel like we're in,

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:44.330 align:start position:0%
the political mess, the cultural
mess, the societal mess,

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.199
do you see a path out of it?

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.803
- That really depends
on us, doesn't it?

00:12:50.803 --> 00:12:52.371
Because we all have
to make the choice

00:12:52.371 --> 00:12:54.507 align:start size:84% position:16%
about how we show
up every single day,

00:12:54.507 --> 00:12:58.144
and if people don't want
to show up in an adult way,

00:12:58.144 --> 00:12:59.378
then they're not going to,

00:12:59.378 --> 00:13:01.180
if people don't wanna
have conversations

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.015
with people they disagree
with, they're not going to.

00:13:03.015 --> 00:13:05.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think my greatest
fear in this whole thing is

00:13:05.985 --> 00:13:07.787
that it seems as though
there are so many people

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:09.421
that are just addicted to anger

00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:12.825
and outrage and fighting, and
that is a physical addiction,

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:14.460
that is an addiction
just like cigarettes

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.795
or drugs or alcohol

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:18.197
and so in order to get
past that addiction,

00:13:18.197 --> 00:13:20.099
they have to want
to overcome it,

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:22.935
and I worry that there
aren't enough people

00:13:22.935 --> 00:13:24.203
that want to overcome it,

00:13:24.203 --> 00:13:26.505 align:start size:88% position:13%
but again I'm on the
ground every single week

00:13:26.505 --> 00:13:27.973
at WalkAway rallies

00:13:27.973 --> 00:13:30.042 align:start position:0%
and I see that there are so
many people that are being kind,

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:32.578 align:start size:88% position:13%
and like truly kind, not
left is kind of kind,

00:13:32.578 --> 00:13:34.280
but truly kind and empathetic

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.748
and understanding to each other

00:13:35.748 --> 00:13:37.917
that it really does give
me hope that it's possible,

00:13:37.917 --> 00:13:39.752
but we're gonna have to
see after the election.

00:13:39.752 --> 00:13:41.353
I don't think we're gonna
get there before November,

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.922
but maybe afterwards.

00:13:42.922 --> 00:13:44.390
- Well, I'm with you, of course.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.826
And I guess I was sort
of like the original YLF,

00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:48.694 align:start size:84% position:16%
the left guy, but
then when I see people

00:13:48.694 --> 00:13:50.129
like you out there, I'm like,

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:52.998
"Oh, it's real, it's real

00:13:52.998 --> 00:13:55.467 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it's happening with
other people and it's great".

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:58.337
So Karlyn pimp it out,
pimp out your Locals,

00:13:58.337 --> 00:13:59.471
why should people join?

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:02.608
- Yeah, they should join
because it's just a group

00:14:02.608 --> 00:14:04.577
of a regular people
that we get together,

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:07.279
